!XuArray methodsFor: #'bulk accessing'!
{XuArray} copy: count {XuIntValue default: DefaultMinusOne} with: start {XuIntValue default: DefaultZero} with: before {XuIntValue default: DefaultZero} with: after {XuIntValue default: DefaultZero} 

	"Make a copy of a piece of this array.  'Count' defaults to the count of the array minus 'start'.  'start' defaults to the beginning of the array, so with arguments, copy just copies the entire array.  'Before' and 'after' both default to 0.  They describe the count of nulls/0s to be added in the result array before the copied elements or after the copied elements.  For example, to copy everything after 10 into a new array leaving room for 20 elements, the incantation would be:
		array->copy(-1,10,20)"
	
	| retVal {XuArray} |
	(self isBroken) ifTrue:
		[^XuArray makeBrokenBy: self].
	(count isBroken) ifTrue:
		[^XuArray makeBrokenBy: count].
	(start isBroken) ifTrue:
		[^XuArray makeBrokenBy: start].
	(before isBroken) ifTrue:
		[^XuArray makeBrokenBy: before].
	(after isBroken) ifTrue:
		[^XuArray makeBrokenBy: after].

	Heaper problems.AllBlasts 
		handle: [:ex | retVal _ XuArray makeBroken: ex asProblem. ex return]
		do: 	[retVal _ XuArray make: (self getActualPrimArray copy:count getActualInt32 with:start getActualInt32 with:before getActualInt32 with:after getActualInt32)].
	XuPromise inDelayBlock ifFalse:
		[XuPromise force.
		retVal isBroken ifTrue: [retVal explode]].
	^retVal! !

